<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- June 27-29.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- June 27-29.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final</p>
<p>data for the top 10 movies at the June 27-29 box office,</p>
<p>according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film			Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Face/Off		     $23,387,530	 $  ----</p>
<p>2. Hercules		     $21,454,451	 $ 23,658,555</p>
<p>3. Batman &amp; Robin	     $15,735,702	 $ 75,208,048</p>
<p>4. My Best Friend's Wedding $15,016,921	 $ 49,220,136</p>
<p>5. Con Air			$ 5,898,935	 $ 78,549,925</p>
<p>6. The Lost World	     $ 4,536,180	 $213,223,429</p>
<p>7. Speed 2: Cruise Control  $ 3,726,336	 $ 38,112,684</p>
<p>8. Liar Liar		    $ 1,303,400	 $172,929,215</p>
<p>9. Austin Powers		$   671,090	 $ 49,981,181</p>
<p>10 Gone Fishin'		 $   632,997	 $ 17,351,349</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Face/Off&quot; is released by Paramont Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Hercules,&quot; &quot;Con Air&quot; and &quot;Gone Fishin'&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co..</p>
<p>&quot;Batman &amp; Robin&quot; is released by Warner Bros, a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;My Best Friend's Wedding&quot; is released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;The Lost World: Jurassic Park&quot; and &quot;Liar Liar&quot; are released by Universal Studios, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Speed 2: Cruise Control&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner.</p>
</text>
